Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:42:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Lower gateway profiler default to 25 Hz after live
 50 Hz overrun

The post-deploy no-override live check at the 50 Hz default measured the
gateway-profiler thread at 1.3854%, 3.6331% and 3.3729% of one core
(123/166/149 threads), missing the <3% acceptance on two of three runs.
Explicit 25 Hz live probes measured 1.7418%, 1.8144% and 2.1481%
(147/152/171 threads).

- DEFAULT_HZ = 25 in gateway/control_profile.py, used when a control
  request omits hz; the CLI --hz default is 25 (parity test enforced).
- Explicit hz 10..200 still overrides; CPU refresh stays 0.1 s.
- Benchmark --hz now defaults to omitting hz, so it exercises the same
  default path as a live request, and records the effective hz.
- New control-socket test: omitted hz -> hz 25, <=26 samples/s; explicit
  50 -> >26 samples. Default tests were RED on the 50 Hz code.
- Docs record the live shortfall, the 40 ms vs 20 ms stack-resolution
  cost, synthetic 25 vs 50 Hz A/B, and keep earlier history intact.

The required no-override live acceptance must be re-run after deploy;
25 Hz probes are not that acceptance.
